#basePath P3_TroutPop
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Start
@exposed
@cutscene

// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P3_TroutPop"


//checks to see if the player has chosen to look at trout population first
$if global:ciscoFirst == false
$set global:troutFirst = true
$endif

//varies dialogue depending on whether the player talked to Renato first
$if global:troutFirst == true
{Renato}   
       I've see you've decided to ditch my brother for me. 
       Always a great sight.
$elseif global: troutFirst == false
{@Renato}
       Finished talking to my brother? He sure knows how to talk. 
$endif

{@Renato}
       It's the population numbers for trout that you need, right?
       The other fishers and I have been looking through the data, recently. 
       It's been falling since the last few years. 
       Currently, its at about 23 million trout. But who knows what that'll be in the future.
$call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-Lake-Trout")

{@You}
       That's...disheartening. Thanks for the information, though.

$if global:troutFirst == true
{@You}
       I wonder if adding more fish to the lake could potentially help with the decrease.

{@Renato}
       It might be worth looking into. 
       There's an aquaculture facility nearby that might be able to help.

{@You}
       That's a good idea. I should check it out. 
       Or I could talk to João. Let's see...
$endif

$call UnlockLocation(FishHatchery)
$call SetTravelTime(FishHatchery, 1)
$call EnableMapButton()
$call CheckIfOutOfTime()


:: AtFishHatchery
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_TroutPop", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "FishHatchery"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()


//Changes dialogue depending on whether stock cisco is already done
$if global:stockCisco == true
{@}
       Neveah is still looking over the pools. 

{@Neveah}
       Come back for more? A nice picnic with the fishies?
{@You}
       Sorry, no fish picnic at the moment, but I need your help with something else.

{@Neveah}
       What's up?

{@You}
       You know how you told me cisco can be added back into the lake.
       I was wondering if that would also be possible with trout?

{Neveah}
       Ooo, yes, definitely. 
       Here, come look at their tank.

{@}
       She guides you over to another tank. 

{@Neveah}
       Hi, babies. 
       These are trout. Five months old. 
       We can definitely add them to the lake, if you'd like. 
$call GiveActionCard("Action-stock-lake-trout")

{@You}
       That would be amazing. 
       Thanks for your help. 

{@Neveah}
       Of course, friend!
       Oh, and about that free portrait that I told you about earlier...

{@}
       She hands you a small canvas, barely larger than your palm. 
       It's a sea lamprey. 

{@Neveah}
       You said you didn't have any pets. 
       So, I figured this was the next best thing. 

{@}
       You think about the torn photo in your pocket, but it's less heavy.

{@You}
       This is beautiful, Neveah. 
       Thank you. Really.

{@}
       She pulls you into a tight hug. 
       Back in your car, you put the photo on the dash, and the sea lamprey almost seems to smile at you. 
$elseif global:stockCisco == false
{@}
       The hatchery is... different than what you imagined. 
       Rows of deep pools remind you of your university's Olympic swimming pool.
       But with the mass of athletes replaced with tighly-packed scales.
       At the edge of one of the rows, an aquaculture specialist looks lovingly into the water.

{@Specialist}
       Hello, George. Hello, Henrietta. Hello, Sir Troutsalot. 

{@You}
       Um, hello?

{@Specialist}
       Ooo, hi there. Wanna look at the fish?

{@You}
       You know what, yes, I do.

{@}
       You join her at the edge of the pool and peer into the water.

{@Specialist}
       These are trout. Five months old. 
       I'm Neveah, by the way!

{@You}
       Ana. I've actually come to talk to you about the trout.

{@Neveah}
       I'd love to talk about my fish children. 
       That's what I call them. The trout.

{@You}
       Makes sense.
       Have you ever released these fish into the wild?

{@Neveah}
       Ooo, yes, we've done that before! 
       It's been helpful to the population in the lake in the past.

{@You}   
       Well, that's good news. 
       Do you think that would be possible to do now?
       
{@Neveah}
       Oh, definitely. 
       I'm sure you'll take excellent care of my fishies.
$call GiveActionCard("Action-stock-lake-trout")

{@You}
       I'll definitely do my best. 

{@Neveah}
       Yay! That's a plan, then. 
       Oooo, I'm very excited. Do you have any fish?

{@You}
       Uhhh, no. 

{@Neveah}
       Aw, man. I do fish portraiture. Very glamorous. 
       I'd like to give you a portrait, but if you don't have a pet...
       I'll figure something out!

{@You}
       Oh, no, no, you really don't have to.

{@Neveah}
       Nope, too late!
       Okay, bye bye now. I've got trout to look after!

{@}
       Before you have time to say anything, she's back to greeting the fish. 

$set global:stockTrout = true
$endif

// skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P3_Hub.Continue